WEBVTT

00:00:00.703 --> 00:00:01.630
Hello everyone.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.630
In this job, there is one sentence that is very hard to say:

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:08.830
I am sorry, I cannot do this for you today.

00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:13.115
It is hard to say, because the client has already come all the way in,

00:00:13.065 --> 00:00:14.830
and because we need clients too.

00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:17.790
But knowing when not to work is also part of your skill.

00:00:18.188 --> 00:00:19.950
This lesson covers three things:

00:00:20.276 --> 00:00:24.786
looking and asking before you start, the signs that mean you must stop,

00:00:24.736 --> 00:00:26.670
and how to decline gracefully.

00:00:27.314 --> 00:00:29.399
Let me tell you about something that happens a lot.

00:00:29.804 --> 00:00:33.590
A client comes in for her nails, and one nail is slightly greenish,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.318
and a little lifted at the tip.

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:36.919
The technician thinks:

00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:38.599
a dark polish will cover it.

00:00:39.102 --> 00:00:43.492
A few weeks later, the client comes back, the nail has lifted even more,

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:44.999
and she blames the salon.

00:00:45.439 --> 00:00:47.239
The polish did not cure anything.

00:00:47.651 --> 00:00:50.119
It only hid the problem, until it got worse.

00:00:50.364 --> 00:00:54.106
And the tools used that day, if they were not processed carefully,

00:00:54.056 --> 00:00:56.119
will carry germs to the next client.

00:00:56.721 --> 00:01:00.285
That is why, before every service, you do two things:

00:01:00.551 --> 00:01:01.965
look, and ask.

00:01:02.225 --> 00:01:05.636
Look in good light, while the skin and nails are still clean,

00:01:05.586 --> 00:01:07.565
with no polish and nothing applied.

00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:12.205
Then ask a few short questions, and write the answers on the consultation form.

00:01:12.756 --> 00:01:13.965
Do you have any allergies?

00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:18.365
Are you taking any medication, or having any treatment for your skin or eyes?

00:01:18.604 --> 00:01:19.725
Do you have diabetes?

00:01:19.893 --> 00:01:22.605
Have you recently had surgery, or any infection?

00:01:23.114 --> 00:01:26.765
Ask regular clients again too, because health changes over time.

00:01:27.377 --> 00:01:30.292
There is one principle I want you to remember very well:

00:01:30.627 --> 00:01:32.772
a technician does not diagnose.

00:01:33.085 --> 00:01:34.372
We are not doctors.

00:01:34.476 --> 00:01:35.332
Never say:

00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:37.172
you have a fungal infection.

00:01:37.581 --> 00:01:38.532
Say what you see:

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.964
I can see this nail has changed color and thickened,

00:01:41.914 --> 00:01:44.292
I think it would be best to let a doctor,

00:01:44.449 --> 00:01:46.372
or a pharmacist, look at it first.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:50.452
Describe what you see, advise a medical visit, and stop there.

00:01:51.085 --> 00:01:52.231
Why do I stress this?

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.111
Because by eye alone, nobody can be sure.

00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:59.605
A thick, yellowish nail could be a fungus, or psoriasis,

00:01:59.555 --> 00:02:01.831
or simply years of tight shoes.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.551
Some of these are contagious, some are not.

00:02:05.059 --> 00:02:07.671
Telling them apart is the job of a health professional.

00:02:07.991 --> 00:02:12.311
Our job is to notice that something is not normal, and to stop at the right moment.

00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:14.636
Now let me go through each trade.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:15.756
Nails:

00:02:15.862 --> 00:02:18.716
a nail that turns green, yellow or brown.

00:02:19.144 --> 00:02:22.156
A nail that thickens, becomes brittle and crumbles.

00:02:22.579 --> 00:02:24.476
A nail that separates from the nail bed.

00:02:24.823 --> 00:02:29.596
Skin around the nail that is swollen, red, painful, or has pus.

00:02:29.905 --> 00:02:31.676
Warts, and open wounds.

00:02:32.158 --> 00:02:36.876
When you see these signs, do not work on that nail, or on that area of skin.

00:02:37.071 --> 00:02:40.796
With the feet of a client who has diabetes, be extra careful.

00:02:40.971 --> 00:02:45.035
The feet may have reduced feeling, and a scratch heals very slowly.

00:02:45.422 --> 00:02:50.716
Water only lukewarm, no long soaking, no blades, no cutting the skin.

00:02:51.305 --> 00:02:54.667
If the foot has an ulcer or a wound, do not work on it,

00:02:54.617 --> 00:02:56.956
and advise the client to see a doctor,

00:02:57.064 --> 00:02:58.476
or a foot care specialist.

00:02:59.106 --> 00:03:00.320
Lashes and brows:

00:03:00.509 --> 00:03:04.640
eyes that are red, itchy, watery, or with sticky discharge.

00:03:04.949 --> 00:03:09.040
A stye, or eyelid rims that are red, swollen and crusty.

00:03:09.707 --> 00:03:13.547
A client who has just had eye surgery, or recently had an eye infection,

00:03:13.497 --> 00:03:15.600
waits until the doctor says it is fine.

00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:19.378
If you see tiny specks clinging to the base of the lashes,

00:03:19.328 --> 00:03:21.840
and the lashes are very itchy, stop as well.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:27.840
And a client who has reacted before to lash glue or lash tint is not treated again with that product.

00:03:28.022 --> 00:03:31.680
I covered allergies in detail in the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:03:32.324 --> 00:03:33.447
Hair and scalp:

00:03:33.763 --> 00:03:36.567
head lice, and their eggs stuck to the hair shafts.

00:03:36.837 --> 00:03:39.127
Sores or open wounds on the scalp.

00:03:39.476 --> 00:03:42.007
Round, red, scaly patches.

00:03:42.418 --> 00:03:45.207
Or heavy hair loss in patches, for no clear reason.

00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:49.367
If you find lice, do not panic, and do not say it out loud.

00:03:49.714 --> 00:03:53.687
Stop, tell the client privately, and suggest a visit to the pharmacy.

00:03:54.036 --> 00:03:58.727
Then wash the towels, and process the combs, scissors and cape thoroughly.

00:03:59.283 --> 00:04:01.612
Skin, spa and waxing:

00:04:01.981 --> 00:04:03.132
sunburned skin.

00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:06.092
Scratched skin, or skin that is infected.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.852
Cold sores on the lips.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.852
Rashes that may be contagious.

00:04:10.326 --> 00:04:13.532
For waxing, there is one question you must always ask:

00:04:13.961 --> 00:04:17.372
are you using any acne medication, or a retinoid cream?

00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:21.691
The acne tablet isotretinoin makes the skin thin and fragile,

00:04:21.641 --> 00:04:24.172
and waxing can lift off a layer of skin.

00:04:24.426 --> 00:04:29.612
If the client is taking it, or stopped within about the last six months, do not wax.

00:04:29.797 --> 00:04:34.812
For creams, follow the instructions of the wax brand, and of the prescribing doctor.

00:04:35.431 --> 00:04:36.731
Now the hardest part:

00:04:37.049 --> 00:04:37.931
how to say it.

00:04:38.437 --> 00:04:42.731
First, speak privately and quietly, so other clients cannot hear.

00:04:43.236 --> 00:04:47.451
Second, talk about the safety of the client, not about your own fears.

00:04:47.793 --> 00:04:48.651
For example:

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.221
I want you to look beautiful and stay safe,

00:04:51.171 --> 00:04:53.291
so I would rather not do this area today.

00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:55.611
Finally, offer another way:

00:04:55.882 --> 00:04:58.723
do the other nails, switch to a different service,

00:04:58.673 --> 00:05:01.291
or book again once the doctor says it is fine.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.651
Do not look disgusted, and do not step back.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.251
The client will remember your attitude in that moment for a long time.

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:10.334
Some clients will plead:

00:05:10.673 --> 00:05:14.014
it is fine, just do it, I take responsibility.

00:05:14.417 --> 00:05:15.614
You still do not do it.

00:05:16.114 --> 00:05:19.774
That promise will not make red eyes clear up, or make a wound heal.

00:05:20.181 --> 00:05:21.374
Gently say again:

00:05:21.802 --> 00:05:24.254
I am saying no because I care about you.

00:05:24.926 --> 00:05:27.553
Afterwards, make a note in the client record:

00:05:27.813 --> 00:05:30.753
the date, what you saw, and what you advised.

00:05:31.104 --> 00:05:34.113
Write only what you saw, not the name of a disease.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.001
This is health information, and it is private,

00:05:36.951 --> 00:05:39.633
so only record it with the consent of the client,

00:05:39.822 --> 00:05:41.633
and keep it strictly confidential.

00:05:41.983 --> 00:05:45.553
And if you are unsure whether to go ahead or not, the answer is:

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.433
do not.

00:05:46.674 --> 00:05:50.673
Losing one appointment today is better than losing the reputation of the whole salon.

00:05:51.331 --> 00:05:52.848
There is also the other side:

00:05:53.028 --> 00:05:55.408
sometimes it is the technician who should not work.

00:05:55.736 --> 00:05:58.208
A small, clean scratch on your hand:

00:05:58.547 --> 00:06:01.488
cover it with a waterproof plaster, then wear gloves.

00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:07.289
But if a wound on your hand is swollen, red, or has pus, do not touch clients,

00:06:07.239 --> 00:06:08.448
and see a doctor.

00:06:08.952 --> 00:06:14.884
If you have a fever, diarrhea, vomiting, pink eye, or any contagious illness,

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:15.648
stay home.

00:06:15.897 --> 00:06:18.448
Salon owners should also tell their staff clearly:

00:06:18.631 --> 00:06:20.448
reporting sick is not a fault.

00:06:21.059 --> 00:06:23.968
Declining at the right moment does not lose you clients.

00:06:24.224 --> 00:06:28.725
People who are told the truth, and allowed to keep their dignity, usually come back,

00:06:28.675 --> 00:06:30.368
and trust you more than before.

00:06:30.945 --> 00:06:32.973
Rules differ from country to country,

00:06:32.923 --> 00:06:35.968
and this lesson does not replace the advice of a doctor.

00:06:36.304 --> 00:06:38.848
And now, take the quiz below the video.
